Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'routing: Availability and DNC List were shown to every user and reachable by none. Neither nav item carries adminOnly, so the sidebar offered both to an advisor, but both routes were wrapped in ProtectedRoute requireAdmin whose denial branch was Navigate to slash replace - so clicking either landed the user back on Overview, which from their side is indistinguishable from a dead button. That is why it was reported as a routing bug rather than a permission one. Both guards were also STRICTER THAN THE API they call and were therefore protecting nothing: compliance_router says in its own comments that GET suppression-list is require_tenant_user, ALL users can view, and POST is ALL users can add, with only permanent-dnc and delete requiring admin; availability_router has no admin requirement anywhere and scopes every endpoint to the calling advisor, since that page is where an FSA sets their own hours. Both pages already gate their admin-only sections internally - Compliance even renders an explanation for non-admins that the route guard made unreachable dead code - so those sections are unchanged and still hidden. Separately, every role refusal now RENDERS a refusal instead of redirecting home: new pages/AccessState.jsx gives an Unauthorized state naming the level required and the level held, keeping the Layout so the screen is not a dead end and leaving the URL alone so a refresh gives the same honest answer, and a NotFound state so an unknown URL stops silently pretending it was Overview and hiding broken links from us. The platform area is the one deliberate exception: it answers not-found rather than naming itself, because a tenant user reaches it only by guessing a URL and a you-need-god_admin refusal would confirm the guess. No server-side permission changed. Also fixes a date-dependent flake in smoke_scheduling that blocked this deploy: next_weekday counts from TOMORROW, so running ON a Monday returns the Monday a full seven days out, and a seven-day minimum notice does not hide a day exactly seven days away. The assertion passed Tuesday through Sunday and failed every Monday. The notice window is now derived from how far the target day actually is rather than hardcoded.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
